Release Notes unified i.MX6 Linux BSP:
======================================
 
BSP-Yocto-i.MX6-PD16.1.0                2017-01-23
--------------------------------------------------
- Linux Kernel v4.1.36 (v4.1 is a LTS kernel)
 * Update from v4.1.18 to v4.1.36
 * linux-mainline: CVE-2016-8655 https://lwn.net/Articles/708319/
 * linux-mainline: CVE-2016-5195 (Dirty Cow) https://heise.de/-3355996
- barebox v2016.11.0
 * Update barebox NAND layout. Using ubi static volums for kernel and devicetree
- Yocto 2.1.2 (krogoth)
- Qt 5.6.2 from meta-qt5 (krogoth)

Tested Yocto Images:
--------------------
- phytec-qt5demo-image

Build Environment:
------------------
- Ubuntu 14.04 64Bit

New Configuration:
------------------
- Added support for new machines:
  * phyboard-mira-imx6-6
  * phyboard-mira-imx6-9
  * phyboard-mira-imx6-10
  * phyboard-mira-imx6-11
  * phyboard-mira-imx6-12

New Features:
-------------
- barebox/yocto: env refactoring in barebox-env in meta-phytec
- barebox: nv variables are saved automatically on shutdown
- implemenet DA9062 and DA9063 Watchdog and reboot handler for phyFLEX and phyCORE
  in kernel and barebox watchdog is not enable by default
- Enable double buffering in i.MX6 OpenGL Library and Qt
- update vivante GPU library for i.MX6 QuadPLus
- VM-012 support (vita1300)
- RS485 Support
- gstreamer: add kmssink
- gstreamer: add v4l2 encoder for i.MX6 VPU
- gstreamer: add bayer2rgb-neon
- tuxracer recipe in meta-yogurt
- bvtest: crop support

Fixed Issues:
-------------
- Fix: i.MX6 DualLite/Solo Stability Issue at 396 Mhz.
    Linux kernel patch "ARM: dts: imx6dl: Fix the VDD_ARM_CAP voltage for 396MHz operation".
    Fixes Phytec's LPN-226e_1.
- fix phyCORE-i.MX6 stability (PMIC buckets)
- linux-mainline: fix Micrel ethernet phy link detection issues at -30°C
- linux-mainline: fix VM-010-BW and VM-010-COL for phyBOARD-SUBRA

Known Issues:
-------------
- CAN is not working with 10 kbaud (also didn´t work in previous releases)
- Display and HDMI do not work with the QuadPlus

Notes:
------
 
Updating the kernel, device tree and rootfs has changed in this release. As kernel and device tree are now placed
in a static ubi volume inside the rootfs partition.
Following example shows how to update those parts in NAND from Network with the new barebox loaded:
 
 bootloader$ ubiformat -y /dev/nand0.root
 bootloader$ ubiattach /dev/nand0.root
 
 bootloader$ ubimkvol -t static /dev/nand0.root.ubi kernel 8M
 bootloader$ ubimkvol -t static /dev/nand0.root.ubi oftree 1M
 bootloader$ ubimkvol -t dynamic /dev/nand0.root.ubi root 0
 
 bootloader$ ubiupdatevol /dev/nand0.root.ubi.kernel /mnt/tftp/linuximage
 bootloader$ ubiupdatevol /dev/nand0.root.ubi.oftree /mnt/tftp/oftree
 bootloader$ cp /mnt/tftp/rootfs.ubifs /dev/nand0.root.ubi.root
